{
  "configuration_id": "config_048",
  "reason": "The current best (config_036, 0.7150 acc) uses scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l with avgpool and concat. The largest single-variable gains so far came from switching the image encoder (resnet50→ViT, +8.4%) and the RNA encoder (PCA→scvi, +1.3%). However, the scgpt RNA encoder has never been tested in any experiment, making it the biggest remaining uncertainty in the design space. config_048 changes only the RNA encoder from scvi_n200 to scgpt while holding all other settings at their empirically best values (multiprofile, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, concat). This cleanly isolates whether scgpt's generative pretraining yields a meaningfully different RNA representation than scvi's VAE. If scgpt outperforms scvi_n200, it opens a new exploitation direction; if it underperforms, it confirms scvi_n200 is near-optimal and redirects budget toward aggregation/fusion refinements. Under a limited budget, resolving this high-impact, zero-information variable is more valuable than a smaller incremental change (e.g., testing weighted fusion or transformer aggregation) whose expected effect is already partially constrained by prior evidence."
}

